1
00:00:01,620 --> 00:00:03,430
Look, Tsubomi.

2
00:00:03,950 --> 00:00:06,150
When you make frogs float,
they start swimming.

3
00:00:06,440 --> 00:00:08,770
Wow, how cute.

4
00:00:08,770 --> 00:00:11,310
I can make the bar all squishy.

5
00:00:11,310 --> 00:00:13,190
You're amazing, Mob-kun.

6
00:00:17,640 --> 00:00:19,840
That's the evening chime. Let's go home.

7
00:00:19,840 --> 00:00:21,470
That was so much fun!

8
00:00:31,010 --> 00:00:33,360
Oh... it was just a dream.

9
00:00:42,376 --> 00:00:44,086
(MOB MOB WOW!)

10
00:00:45,206 --> 00:00:46,956
(MOB MOB WOW!)

11
00:00:48,126 --> 00:00:49,796
(MOB MOB WOW!)

12
00:00:50,966 --> 00:00:52,636
(MOB MOB WOW!)

13
00:00:54,046 --> 00:00:56,766
I realized that our youth is gray

14
00:00:56,766 --> 00:00:59,686
The origin of this uneasiness
Is yet unknown

15
00:00:59,766 --> 00:01:02,186
Trains of emotions keep running
Through my brain

16
00:01:02,186 --> 00:01:05,356
Struggling through this adolescence

17
00:01:05,476 --> 00:01:08,316
Don't disturb my deep psyche

18
00:01:08,316 --> 00:01:10,986
Who is that behind you?

19
00:01:11,106 --> 00:01:14,776
Opposing ideas creates distortion

20
00:01:14,776 --> 00:01:18,196
Exorcise all the sorrow

21
00:01:18,366 --> 00:01:21,866
So, do what you can now

22
00:01:21,956 --> 00:01:23,786
My life

23
00:01:24,036 --> 00:01:27,916
Finally, break it down

24
00:01:29,416 --> 00:01:32,256
(Want) Both greed
(Young) And honesty

25
00:01:32,256 --> 00:01:35,136
(Burn) Are growing
(1) On this chest of mine

26
00:01:35,136 --> 00:01:37,886
(Trance) I'm not waking up
(Chance) I want to wake up

27
00:01:37,886 --> 00:01:40,846
(Stance) These two different faces of mine
(1) Are standing back-to-back

28
00:01:40,846 --> 00:01:43,346
Taking things as it is

29
00:01:43,346 --> 00:01:46,766
In this free relation where
We resent each other

30
00:01:46,856 --> 00:01:49,066
Once these two become one

31
00:01:49,066 --> 00:01:51,066
That smile becomes one

32
00:01:51,066 --> 00:01:54,156
And only "1"
(MOB MOB WOW!)

33
00:01:54,816 --> 00:01:57,826
"1"
(MOB MOB WOW!)

34
00:01:58,156 --> 00:01:59,236
(MOB MOB WOW!)

35
00:01:59,236 --> 00:02:02,116
One and only "1"
(MOB MOB WOW!)

36
00:02:02,286 --> 00:02:03,826
"1"

37
00:02:03,826 --> 00:02:04,996
(MOB MOB WOW!)

38
00:02:04,996 --> 00:02:07,286
One and only "1"

39
00:02:08,980 --> 00:02:13,480
(Mob 1
~Moving~)

40
00:02:13,480 --> 00:02:15,140
Happy New Year!

41
00:02:15,649 --> 00:02:17,130
Did you go somewhere during break?

42
00:02:17,130 --> 00:02:18,780
My grandma's place.

43
00:02:20,140 --> 00:02:21,540
Did you finish it?

44
00:02:21,540 --> 00:02:23,360
Yeah, I did.

45
00:02:28,330 --> 00:02:30,060
Happy New Year.

46
00:02:30,060 --> 00:02:32,080
We start the third term today.

47
00:02:32,470 --> 00:02:34,960
I'll be collecting your
homework from winter break

48
00:02:34,960 --> 00:02:37,750
after the opening assembly today.

49
00:02:38,090 --> 00:02:40,270
You all need to get over
the winter-break slump

50
00:02:40,270 --> 00:02:42,730
and start studying
for your entrance exams.

51
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:45,720
Make sure you all work hard together
while you're still classmates.

52
00:02:45,720 --> 00:02:48,000
Oh, the class shuffles.

53
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:52,050
Maybe when I become a third-year,
I'll be in the same class as Tsubomi.

54
00:02:52,050 --> 00:02:55,200
Oh, I have one more announcement to make.

55
00:02:55,770 --> 00:02:59,770
Takane Tsubomi from Class 3
will be moving next month.

56
00:03:01,290 --> 00:03:02,230
What?

57
00:03:02,870 --> 00:03:05,220
Huh? Moving...?

58
00:03:06,130 --> 00:03:08,020
Wait, what?

59
00:03:08,670 --> 00:03:11,050
This is so sudden that
my head can't keep up.

60
00:03:11,410 --> 00:03:12,090
What?

61
00:03:12,090 --> 00:03:16,550
I mean, I was planning to tell her how I
feel after entrance exam season was over.

62
00:03:16,550 --> 00:03:20,790
But... I mean... I was still
supposed to have another year...

63
00:03:20,790 --> 00:03:22,670
No, really, wait...

64
00:03:22,980 --> 00:03:25,920
I haven't... I haven't even
gotten to do anything yet.

65
00:03:25,920 --> 00:03:27,860
Nothing's... happened.

66
00:03:30,850 --> 00:03:33,410
I need to... ask her out.

67
00:03:34,420 --> 00:03:37,080
What's the matter, Kageyama?
Did you forget your homework?

68
00:03:37,080 --> 00:03:38,910
Uh, no...

69
00:03:40,550 --> 00:03:42,000
Oh, right...

70
00:03:42,470 --> 00:03:46,540
Mob feels a certain way about Takane-san.

71
00:03:46,540 --> 00:03:47,450
But...

72
00:03:47,452 --> 00:03:51,749
I need to ask her out...

73
00:03:51,750 --> 00:03:54,450
She's the top idol at this school.

74
00:03:54,450 --> 00:03:58,410
How are you gonna take on
all of these rivals, Mob?

75
00:04:02,680 --> 00:04:03,358
(Body Improvement Club)

76
00:04:03,360 --> 00:04:06,080
A-Ask her out?!

77
00:04:07,090 --> 00:04:08,170
Yes...

78
00:04:08,170 --> 00:04:10,090
Are you sane, Kageyama?!

79
00:04:10,390 --> 00:04:11,470
So...

80
00:04:13,180 --> 00:04:14,990
I was hoping you could tell me
your experiences,

81
00:04:14,990 --> 00:04:16,840
or how to make sure I don't upset her...

82
00:04:16,840 --> 00:04:18,490
Advice like that!

83
00:04:18,490 --> 00:04:19,720
Experiences?

84
00:04:21,630 --> 00:04:22,840
Kageyama!

85
00:04:23,270 --> 00:04:25,410
You're the shadow leader at Salt Middle!

86
00:04:25,660 --> 00:04:29,870
Grow a pair! Show her what
White T Poison's made of!

87
00:04:30,370 --> 00:04:31,350
Sorry?

88
00:04:31,720 --> 00:04:32,750
Er, just... You know...

89
00:04:33,080 --> 00:04:36,850
Show her White T Poison's...
uh, made of...

90
00:04:40,460 --> 00:04:43,620
Kageyama... Take off your clothes.

91
00:04:43,620 --> 00:04:45,550
Huh? Okay.

92
00:04:52,360 --> 00:04:53,810
Ow...

93
00:04:53,810 --> 00:04:56,370
You're developing some
excellent muscles there!

94
00:04:56,370 --> 00:04:59,440
The experience you're looking for
has accumulated in those!

95
00:04:59,440 --> 00:05:01,430
We're seeing the fruits of your labor!

96
00:05:01,430 --> 00:05:04,160
I'm sure that the person
you have in mind will tell you

97
00:05:04,630 --> 00:05:06,260
that your muscles are worthy!

98
00:05:07,530 --> 00:05:09,690
Thank you! Very much!

99
00:05:09,920 --> 00:05:12,930
Let us also strive for
new heights and train!

100
00:05:12,930 --> 00:05:14,680
Yeah!

101
00:05:16,900 --> 00:05:18,650
Body Improvement!

102
00:05:18,650 --> 00:05:22,380
Fight on! Fight on! Fight on!
Fight on! Fight on! Fight on!

103
00:05:28,120 --> 00:05:29,250
Um...

104
00:05:29,510 --> 00:05:31,730
Could I get some advice
on asking her out...?

105
00:05:32,080 --> 00:05:33,310
I'd really appreciate it...

106
00:05:33,920 --> 00:05:35,030
Um...

107
00:05:36,230 --> 00:05:39,890
Like the Brainwave Club could actually
give you advice about asking someone out.

108
00:05:39,890 --> 00:05:41,530
Oh, good point.

109
00:05:41,530 --> 00:05:42,320
Uh, hello?!

110
00:05:43,120 --> 00:05:45,970
But man, I can't believe
Takane is moving.

111
00:05:45,970 --> 00:05:47,770
I've had a crush on her for a while.

112
00:05:48,020 --> 00:05:50,380
Maybe I'll try asking her out, too.

113
00:05:52,530 --> 00:05:56,130
Takenaka, are you planning
on reading Tsubomi's mind?

114
00:05:56,130 --> 00:05:58,380
That would never work for too long,

115
00:05:58,380 --> 00:06:00,430
and I don't plan on
taking out my earplugs.

116
00:06:00,760 --> 00:06:03,640
But if you read a girl's mind,
you could be super popular...

117
00:06:03,640 --> 00:06:05,720
according to Tome-san.

118
00:06:06,590 --> 00:06:10,030
What the heck would President Kurata
know about how a girl feels?

119
00:06:10,030 --> 00:06:12,630
Okay, that's enough, you two!

120
00:06:12,640 --> 00:06:14,890
You sure are running your
mouths while I was frozen

121
00:06:14,890 --> 00:06:16,770
trying to figure out what
the heck's going on.

122
00:06:17,730 --> 00:06:19,310
You're asking her out?

123
00:06:19,310 --> 00:06:21,940
Mob, are you seriously
serious about it this time?

124
00:06:22,240 --> 00:06:23,140
Yes.

125
00:06:23,140 --> 00:06:26,210
I see. All right, then.

126
00:06:26,210 --> 00:06:28,890
I'll give you a piece of very good advice.

127
00:06:30,190 --> 00:06:32,640
You should definitely
change up your hairstyle!

128
00:06:32,640 --> 00:06:35,040
I'll keep the rest of what
I want to say to myself!

129
00:06:35,410 --> 00:06:41,090
Sorry, we can't really offer advice,
so we'll just support you from afar.

130
00:06:41,090 --> 00:06:42,390
I wish you the best.

131
00:06:42,390 --> 00:06:44,370
You've got this, Kageyama!

132
00:06:45,350 --> 00:06:47,810
U-Um, Tsubomi...

133
00:06:48,050 --> 00:06:51,120
I wanted to talk to you
about something. Is that okay?

134
00:06:52,200 --> 00:06:53,480
I-I wuv you...

135
00:06:53,480 --> 00:06:56,390
I wuv you, Tsubomi.
Please go out with me!

136
00:06:56,390 --> 00:06:57,330
I'm sorry.

137
00:06:57,330 --> 00:06:58,780
B-But why?

138
00:06:58,780 --> 00:07:01,980
Oh, do I really need to
tell you the reason?

139
00:07:03,320 --> 00:07:05,830
I mean, I have absolutely
no interest in you...

140
00:07:05,830 --> 00:07:07,450
S-Sorry!

141
00:07:13,230 --> 00:07:16,160
Jeez... There's still that many?

142
00:07:16,160 --> 00:07:18,570
I don't even know most of these people.

143
00:07:20,070 --> 00:07:21,820
What a pain.

144
00:07:36,240 --> 00:07:38,150
What are you doing, Mob?

145
00:07:38,350 --> 00:07:41,040
Takane's not in class anymore.

146
00:07:41,040 --> 00:07:43,100
Oh! Did she go home already?!

147
00:07:43,100 --> 00:07:46,080
I see... She went home...

148
00:07:46,390 --> 00:07:49,330
Then, I guess I'll just have
to give up for today.

149
00:07:49,330 --> 00:07:53,900
Oh, well. I'll just have
to try another day...

150
00:07:53,900 --> 00:07:55,480
She's behind the school.

151
00:07:55,480 --> 00:07:58,110
Behind the school?
What's she doing there?

152
00:07:58,110 --> 00:08:00,960
While you've been wasting your time here,

153
00:08:00,960 --> 00:08:04,090
all the other boys have
been asking her out.

154
00:08:04,940 --> 00:08:06,660
Say what now?

155
00:08:06,660 --> 00:08:08,410
I-I-I better go...

156
00:08:08,890 --> 00:08:11,040
If you go right now,
she's gonna reject you!

157
00:08:11,040 --> 00:08:16,380
It's like some weird factory assembly line
that's producing a bunch of broken-hearted lads.

158
00:08:16,380 --> 00:08:19,490
You'll just get caught up in all that,
and she'll say no to you, too.

159
00:08:24,270 --> 00:08:25,450
Mezato-san...

160
00:08:25,820 --> 00:08:28,910
Do you think I should cut my hair?

161
00:08:28,910 --> 00:08:30,820
Huh? Wait, why your hair?

162
00:08:30,820 --> 00:08:34,790
What kind of guys do girls like?

163
00:08:35,410 --> 00:08:37,830
He's starting to consider
more than just "work out"!

164
00:08:38,220 --> 00:08:40,240
First, you need to be a gentleman.

165
00:08:40,540 --> 00:08:44,140
You should always mind your manners
around all of your girl classmates.

166
00:08:44,590 --> 00:08:47,160
Also, you need to be considerate.

167
00:08:47,450 --> 00:08:50,020
You need to be dependable,
lend an ear to her problems,

168
00:08:50,020 --> 00:08:52,500
and make her think she can
talk about anything.

169
00:08:52,720 --> 00:08:55,710
If you can be that accepting,

170
00:08:55,980 --> 00:08:58,900
you might just be able to
handle Takane, as well.

171
00:08:59,320 --> 00:09:01,670
I'd be able to handle her?

172
00:09:01,910 --> 00:09:02,740
Yeah.

173
00:09:03,110 --> 00:09:07,090
It seems as though most of the guys just
like her because of her appearance,

174
00:09:07,090 --> 00:09:10,270
but I'm pretty sure she's
hiding how she really feels.

175
00:09:10,270 --> 00:09:13,650
It'll be up to you to be able
to handle who she really is.

176
00:09:14,290 --> 00:09:18,900
Though, I honestly don't know
what the big fuss is over Takane.

177
00:09:18,900 --> 00:09:19,580
Huh?

178
00:09:20,020 --> 00:09:23,770
I mean, she doesn't seem
to trust anyone at all.

179
00:09:23,770 --> 00:09:26,620
I'm pretty sure she has
no interest in other people.

180
00:09:26,860 --> 00:09:28,970
How do you know that?

181
00:09:28,970 --> 00:09:31,350
You can tell just by seeing
how she acts every day.

182
00:09:31,350 --> 00:09:33,840
Actually, how can you not tell?

183
00:09:33,840 --> 00:09:38,790
You should learn to view other people
from a different angle every now and then.

184
00:09:41,100 --> 00:09:42,400
Say, Mob...

185
00:09:42,920 --> 00:09:44,780
What exactly do you like about her?

186
00:09:46,390 --> 00:09:49,350
(Spirits and Such Consultation Office)

187
00:09:49,360 --> 00:09:51,540
So... You couldn't respond
to that question,

188
00:09:51,540 --> 00:09:55,330
you couldn't go behind the school,
and you can't fully concentrate on work.

189
00:09:56,670 --> 00:09:58,550
Come on, now, Mob.

190
00:09:58,550 --> 00:10:00,780
Don't go bringing this
puppy love nonsense to work.

191
00:10:01,040 --> 00:10:04,290
Of course middle schoolers
fall in love just by appearances.

192
00:10:04,780 --> 00:10:07,740
I understand why you want to
believe you're different,

193
00:10:07,740 --> 00:10:11,050
but in the end, men are simple creatures.

194
00:10:11,720 --> 00:10:13,040
Am I right, Serizawa?

195
00:10:13,040 --> 00:10:16,750
Er, I didn't go to school,
so I'm not sure.

196
00:10:16,750 --> 00:10:19,310
You must've at least had a girl you liked.

197
00:10:19,310 --> 00:10:21,260
No... I can't say that there was.

198
00:10:21,520 --> 00:10:22,580
Not even one?

199
00:10:23,520 --> 00:10:26,710
Come on, don't be bashful at your age.

200
00:10:27,700 --> 00:10:30,370
No, wait. Are you actually serious?

201
00:10:30,670 --> 00:10:33,550
I'm honestly envious that
you have someone you like.

202
00:10:33,940 --> 00:10:38,140
If your feelings for her don't change,
despite what anyone says...

203
00:10:38,140 --> 00:10:40,780
that means your feelings are true, right?

204
00:10:41,370 --> 00:10:45,570
Then I don't think you have to
put your reasoning into words.

205
00:10:46,240 --> 00:10:50,340
Yes, exactly! That's exactly
what I was trying to say!

206
00:10:50,590 --> 00:10:53,560
What's important is not
what you like about her...

207
00:10:53,560 --> 00:10:56,060
it's if you truly like her or not!

208
00:10:56,320 --> 00:11:00,920
If you're nervous about this,
then tell us how you really feel.

209
00:11:02,830 --> 00:11:03,940
We'll hear you out.

210
00:11:05,900 --> 00:11:10,570
The reason that Tsubomi
caught my attention so much...

211
00:11:12,540 --> 00:11:15,500
Mob! Let's make a tunnel!

212
00:11:15,500 --> 00:11:16,200
Sure.

213
00:11:20,690 --> 00:11:24,420
Look! I'm only showing you, Tsubomi!

214
00:11:25,340 --> 00:11:26,830
I'm bored of that.

215
00:11:27,690 --> 00:11:29,560
I'm not really sure myself.

216
00:11:30,410 --> 00:11:34,710
But I know that I like her.
I've always liked Tsubomi.

217
00:11:35,000 --> 00:11:38,060
Then there's nothing to worry about.

218
00:11:38,060 --> 00:11:39,600
Go for broke.

219
00:11:39,600 --> 00:11:44,950
But I'm not sure what to say
when I ask her out. What should I do?

220
00:11:44,950 --> 00:11:47,360
Well... You know.

221
00:11:48,560 --> 00:11:51,400
First, you wanna be fresh and clean.

222
00:11:51,400 --> 00:11:53,190
Then, remember to be sincere and faithful.

223
00:11:53,190 --> 00:11:56,170
And don't forget to be fashionable
and be a good listener.

224
00:11:56,170 --> 00:11:57,520
Also...

225
00:11:57,760 --> 00:12:00,680
Make sure to smile and don't be glum.

226
00:12:00,680 --> 00:12:02,220
And...

227
00:12:02,220 --> 00:12:06,240
Oh, right. Setting the mood to
excite her is also important.

228
00:12:06,240 --> 00:12:08,360
What?! He's cheating?!

229
00:12:08,360 --> 00:12:09,550
And there you have it!

230
00:12:09,550 --> 00:12:11,820
I guess Reigen-san doesn't know, either.

231
00:12:11,820 --> 00:12:15,830
But in the end...
Don't worry about strategy.

232
00:12:16,130 --> 00:12:18,130
There's no point in trying
to keep up appearances

233
00:12:18,130 --> 00:12:19,840
with a person you want a
deep relationship with.

234
00:12:20,220 --> 00:12:23,680
Just be yourself. Show her your true self.

235
00:12:23,680 --> 00:12:28,460
I'm sure the last thing Tsubomi wants to
hear is you asking her out using my words.

236
00:12:28,840 --> 00:12:31,890
Just put what you're feeling into words.

237
00:12:32,270 --> 00:12:33,980
Thank you very much.

238
00:12:33,980 --> 00:12:36,500
Yes, you're right. I'll do just that.

239
00:12:41,030 --> 00:12:44,270
Reigen, I'm actually a bit
surprised you gave him that advice.

240
00:12:44,270 --> 00:12:49,250
If this were me,
I'd probably try to be slick.

241
00:12:49,250 --> 00:12:52,080
I mean, if they found out
who I really was,

242
00:12:52,080 --> 00:12:55,220
I'd get rejected in an instant.

243
00:12:55,220 --> 00:12:59,110
I guess even Reigen is pessimistic
about these matters.

244
00:12:59,110 --> 00:13:02,690
He seems really popular with our clients
who are older ladies, though...

245
00:13:03,940 --> 00:13:05,010
However...

246
00:13:05,600 --> 00:13:07,020
Mob is different.

247
00:13:07,020 --> 00:13:09,440
He should follow the straight and narrow.

248
00:13:10,080 --> 00:13:12,760
He shouldn't bother with lies.

249
00:13:17,890 --> 00:13:20,190
You've got this, Mob.

250
00:13:33,720 --> 00:13:36,350
What's with all the sighing, friend?

251
00:13:36,970 --> 00:13:39,090
Are you in trouble again?

252
00:13:39,090 --> 00:13:40,530
Hanazawa.

253
00:13:42,710 --> 00:13:45,880
Huh. So your childhood
friend is transferring.

254
00:13:45,880 --> 00:13:46,720
Yeah.

255
00:13:46,720 --> 00:13:49,570
I haven't had the chance to
actually talk to her these past few years,

256
00:13:49,570 --> 00:13:51,590
and this was really sudden.

257
00:13:51,590 --> 00:13:54,520
So that's why you're in
a hurry to ask her out.

258
00:13:54,880 --> 00:13:55,930
Yeah.

259
00:13:56,300 --> 00:13:59,970
But this is my first time,
so it's been pretty difficult.

260
00:13:59,970 --> 00:14:02,660
It's really not something
to be that scared of.

261
00:14:03,070 --> 00:14:05,690
It must be nice being you,
Hanazawa, since you're popular.

262
00:14:05,690 --> 00:14:07,750
You're nothing like me.

263
00:14:08,190 --> 00:14:09,820
What are you talking about?

264
00:14:10,120 --> 00:14:13,770
You're the one who said we
were alike in the first place.

265
00:14:14,170 --> 00:14:17,100
Go on. Relax those shoulders.

266
00:14:17,100 --> 00:14:18,740
Smile and stand proud.

267
00:14:18,740 --> 00:14:23,070
You need to be more confident!
It's not like you're doing anything bad.

268
00:14:24,060 --> 00:14:27,290
Are you thinking about
getting something for her?

269
00:14:27,630 --> 00:14:29,770
That thought hadn't even crossed my mind.

270
00:14:29,770 --> 00:14:32,750
I see... A gift, huh?

271
00:14:33,230 --> 00:14:36,010
I'm usually the one getting asked out,

272
00:14:36,010 --> 00:14:40,430
but when I get letters or homemade cookies,
it does make me pretty happy.

273
00:14:40,430 --> 00:14:42,300
I figured that might be an option.

274
00:14:42,770 --> 00:14:44,120
Homemade...

275
00:14:45,720 --> 00:14:48,580
That's not gonna work.
I only know how to make rice balls.

276
00:14:48,580 --> 00:14:50,820
Hey, you don't need to push yourself.

277
00:14:51,150 --> 00:14:54,700
There's no guarantee that
it's better to give her something.

278
00:14:55,790 --> 00:15:00,940
Actually, in your case, maybe you can get
her some flowers, even if it's a bit cliché.

279
00:15:00,940 --> 00:15:02,600
I'm sure it couldn't hurt.

280
00:15:03,960 --> 00:15:05,530
Flowers...

281
00:15:05,930 --> 00:15:09,130
Also, I'll gladly pick out
your clothes for you.

282
00:15:09,130 --> 00:15:14,120
I don't actually have enough money to
buy any clothes, so I'll pass this time.

283
00:15:14,120 --> 00:15:15,180
Thanks, though.

284
00:15:18,600 --> 00:15:22,120
Brother. About Takane moving...

285
00:15:22,120 --> 00:15:25,240
Oh, you already knew, Ritsu?

286
00:15:26,750 --> 00:15:28,030
I see.

287
00:15:28,330 --> 00:15:31,000
So you're also going to
ask her out, after all.

288
00:15:31,280 --> 00:15:33,550
The time's finally arrived.

289
00:15:33,550 --> 00:15:36,720
I'm honestly really nervous
just thinking about it.

290
00:15:37,590 --> 00:15:39,590
How is she going to respond?

291
00:15:41,710 --> 00:15:46,950
I'm pretty sure I remember Takane-san
saying she likes someone...

292
00:15:47,510 --> 00:15:50,800
Yes. The person I like is someone from
another school who I met at cram school.

293
00:15:51,030 --> 00:15:55,710
From what you've told me, the other person
is obviously interested in you as well.

294
00:15:56,050 --> 00:15:59,100
If you ask them out, there's a very
good possibility they'll say yes.

295
00:15:59,470 --> 00:16:00,790
It's over...

296
00:16:02,170 --> 00:16:06,030
Anyway, I hope she doesn't
turn him down too harshly.

297
00:16:07,090 --> 00:16:08,270
Ritsu...

298
00:16:08,270 --> 00:16:11,870
He's probably more worried
about me than I am.

299
00:16:12,490 --> 00:16:15,630
I'm not sure why, but it
somehow calms me down.

300
00:16:16,400 --> 00:16:19,460
Thanks, Ritsu.
I'll give it everything I've got.

301
00:16:19,460 --> 00:16:20,400
Brother...

302
00:16:21,590 --> 00:16:23,510
Don't lose heart too much, okay?

303
00:16:39,720 --> 00:16:41,810
(Phone Numbers)
(Emergency)

304
00:16:42,180 --> 00:16:43,310
(Takane)

305
00:17:03,950 --> 00:17:05,750
H-Hello?

306
00:17:05,750 --> 00:17:09,710
I-It's been a while, ma'am.
It's me, Shigeo.

307
00:17:10,310 --> 00:17:12,020
Is Tsubomi available?

308
00:17:12,490 --> 00:17:15,520
Y-Yes. Thank you very much.

309
00:17:21,220 --> 00:17:23,810
H-Hello, Tsubomi?

310
00:17:24,260 --> 00:17:28,740
S-Sorry to call you out of the blue.
I only know your house phone.

311
00:17:29,590 --> 00:17:32,110
So, uh, I heard...

312
00:17:32,850 --> 00:17:35,900
Um... Like...

313
00:17:36,340 --> 00:17:38,170
That you're moving away.

314
00:17:38,750 --> 00:17:41,140
Oh... So it's true.

315
00:17:41,990 --> 00:17:43,320
Right, of course.

316
00:17:43,580 --> 00:17:48,560
Yeah, so, hey... There's something
I wanted to talk to you about.

317
00:17:49,290 --> 00:17:52,130
Huh? It's a bit awkward
to say on the phone.

318
00:17:52,720 --> 00:17:56,720
I was wondering if you had some
time after school tomorrow...

319
00:17:56,720 --> 00:17:59,650
No, it's better if we meet
somewhere other than school.

320
00:17:59,650 --> 00:18:03,520
Since we live so close to each other,
why don't we just go to the park?

321
00:18:04,490 --> 00:18:07,600
Yeah. The one we used
to play at all the time.

322
00:18:08,280 --> 00:18:11,180
Hm? I'm acting weird?

323
00:18:11,520 --> 00:18:15,770
Really? My voice? No, it's not shaky...

324
00:18:16,200 --> 00:18:18,730
Yeah... You're totally imagining it.

325
00:18:19,070 --> 00:18:20,680
Yeah, uh-huh.

326
00:18:21,930 --> 00:18:23,070
Yeah, that's fine.

327
00:18:23,980 --> 00:18:25,070
Sure.

328
00:18:37,280 --> 00:18:39,520
What? You made plans with her?

329
00:18:39,520 --> 00:18:40,640
Way to go!

330
00:18:40,940 --> 00:18:42,890
And instead of behind the school,

331
00:18:42,890 --> 00:18:45,710
you chose a nostalgic park
for the both of you. Chef's kiss.

332
00:18:46,550 --> 00:18:48,310
I didn't know you had it in you, man!

333
00:18:48,310 --> 00:18:49,780
If you end up going out with her,

334
00:18:49,780 --> 00:18:52,520
introduce me to one of
Takane's girl friends.

335
00:18:52,770 --> 00:18:53,490
Sure.

336
00:18:53,490 --> 00:18:54,680
Heck yeah!

337
00:18:56,620 --> 00:18:58,200
Now, then...

338
00:18:58,200 --> 00:19:02,438
The point where line A
and line B intersect is -2.

339
00:19:02,440 --> 00:19:04,000
- I wonder what it is...
- This will be on the test.

340
00:19:04,510 --> 00:19:07,630
Despite knowing I'm going to have a really
important conversation with Tsubomi,

341
00:19:07,860 --> 00:19:09,800
I'm surprisingly calm.

342
00:19:12,660 --> 00:19:14,150
Come to think of it,

343
00:19:14,150 --> 00:19:19,700
I wonder why I thought to ask everyone
for advice about asking her out.

344
00:19:25,580 --> 00:19:28,060
I think lately...

345
00:19:28,060 --> 00:19:30,540
I'm not holding in my feelings
as much anymore.

346
00:19:39,030 --> 00:19:42,988
(Seasoning Realty)

347
00:19:42,990 --> 00:19:46,490
(Smiley Flowers)
I'd like an assorted bouquet... please.

348
00:19:46,490 --> 00:19:49,200
(Smiley Flowers)
Sure. Do you need a bag?

349
00:19:50,000 --> 00:19:52,040
Does this work for you?

350
00:19:52,530 --> 00:19:53,670
Yes.

351
00:19:53,670 --> 00:19:56,490
I guess they're really small at 1,000 yen.

352
00:19:56,930 --> 00:19:59,220
It's not about size anyway.

353
00:19:59,850 --> 00:20:01,900
Thank you very much!

354
00:20:06,610 --> 00:20:08,000
Shigeo Kageyama.

355
00:20:10,880 --> 00:20:13,240
Oh... Um, you're...

356
00:20:15,250 --> 00:20:16,900
Trade me.

357
00:20:16,900 --> 00:20:17,620
Huh?!

358
00:20:17,980 --> 00:20:20,320
Are you sure? But why...

359
00:20:20,320 --> 00:20:21,560
Yeah, just come on.

360
00:20:30,950 --> 00:20:31,960
Everyone...

361
00:20:33,236 --> 00:20:34,410
Thank you.

362
00:21:55,370 --> 00:22:00,210
The blue light shined
Dazzling my eye at 01:30 AM

363
00:22:00,250 --> 00:22:05,590
Even as I swiped the page over,
The smiles of friends besides me remain

364
00:22:15,600 --> 00:22:18,020
Yes, I want someone to understand

365
00:22:18,020 --> 00:22:20,520
All the colorless and transparent wishes

366
00:22:20,520 --> 00:22:23,020
All the breath stuck within
The depth of my heart

367
00:22:23,020 --> 00:22:25,650
Suddenly flowed out
Bringing my consciousness back

368
00:22:25,650 --> 00:22:28,110
I remember the days hung dry

369
00:22:28,110 --> 00:22:30,620
The very normal days passed by

370
00:22:30,620 --> 00:22:33,080
Even if reality is corrupted

371
00:22:33,080 --> 00:22:35,830
The sky we saw together
Was definitely real

372
00:22:36,410 --> 00:22:40,540
It's harder to understand than
The grammar on the blackboard

373
00:22:40,540 --> 00:22:45,760
The story that disappears
Under 24 hours makes me sad and lonely

374
00:22:46,010 --> 00:22:50,220
It's so hard, and I find myself
On the verge of giving up again and again

375
00:22:50,220 --> 00:22:51,760
But I...

376
00:22:52,600 --> 00:22:55,930
The current me will no longer give up

377
00:22:56,060 --> 00:23:00,940
Overflowing emotions on my sleeve,
Running through worry and doubt

378
00:23:00,940 --> 00:23:03,573
Nobody has decided
if the future is 0 or 100,

379
00:23:03,575 --> 00:23:06,150
So I'll paint over them myself

380
00:23:06,150 --> 00:23:08,541
Even if my existence itself
can't be proven,

381
00:23:08,543 --> 00:23:11,571
If this world struck me in my heart

382
00:23:11,700 --> 00:23:14,240
I will flood it with cobalt blue

383
00:23:26,120 --> 00:23:30,590
Kageyama, I know that you're
trying to accept your powers.

384
00:23:30,590 --> 00:23:31,630
You've worked so hard.

385
00:23:32,100 --> 00:23:34,260
And that's why
you shouldn't go any further.

386
00:23:34,260 --> 00:23:35,670
Turn back now.

387
00:23:36,030 --> 00:23:38,440
Next time onMob Psycho 100 III Episode 10:

388
00:23:38,440 --> 00:23:40,060
"Mob 2
~Rival~."
